 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Though, in a little walk by Dublin,\nThe ruddy sunbreaks the wondrous fire;\nI have seen it softly gone below him,\nAnd left no trace of himself somewhere;\nBut though he died so far from nobody,\nIt is but you can help to believe him.\nOn a hill above a brazen tower,\nWhich 'tis oft called 'the Tower of Fire,\nThere the great pagodas and towers\nIn their semblance shone (tho' more sublime\nThan those which now inspire us here) above,\nYet where they stood on that sadly above,",
